    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a duplicate-email rejection to `POST /api/owners` that responds **409**, following the existing telephone/household uniqueness pattern exactly rather than inventing a new shape.\n\n**New pieces:**\n- `EnsureUniqueEmail` function \u2014 runs right after `NormalizeOwnerEmail` (so it compares the already-lower-cased value) and before `BuildOwner` persists. Email is optional, so an absent/blank email skips the check; otherwise it throws `DuplicateEmailException` if any owner already has that email.\n- `DuplicateEmailException` (checked, `extends Exception`) and `DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler` (responds 409 with a `ProblemDetail`), plus the escalation YAML that wires them.\n- `findByEmail(String)` added to the `OwnerRepository` interface and all three implementations (Spring Data JPA \u2014 the active profile, plus JPA and JDBC for completeness). The queries compare case-insensitively (`LOWER(email)`) to honor the \"lower-cased email\" spec regardless of stored casing.\n\n**Wiring:** inserted the `ensureUniqueEmail` step into `owners.POST.yml` between `normalizeEmail` and `defaultRegistrationDate`, keeping `govern: [ transaction ]` consistent with its neighbours.\n\nEach class keeps a single responsibility; the uniqueness logic mirrors `EnsureUniqueTelephone` rather than being bolted onto an existing step. The `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` case and the full suite pass.",
